nce; screenshot-measures-the-window fixed by injected content-height (1028px → 929px) | 2026-08-16.md | 2026-08-16 |\n| [[concepts/closeout-scope-discipline-other-sessions-work]] | Closeout sweeps this session's surface only: another session's 7 untracked files left alone, push authorized for KeystoneOS only, self-reported SecondBrain push, and the unsent report #1 caught against KR 4.1 | 2026-08-16.md | 2026-08-16 |\n| [[concepts/backup-error-log-recurring-failures-2026-08-16]] | `repo-diverged:SecondBrain` since 8/12, `snapshot:sessions`, and `manifest-unmanaged` for five ~/DEV folders; divergence escalated to `/claude-stack-doctor` rather than guessed at | 2026-08-16.md | 2026-08-16 |\n| [[connections/fix-the-sentence-everywhere-it-was-copied]] | Text propagates across siblings, across edit-pass time, and across generated/authored seams; fix along the propagation graph and disclose sibling fixes that exceed approved scope | 2026-08-16.md | 2026-08-16 |\n| [[concepts/layout-assumptions-break-on-viewport-change]] | A design-direction change is a bulk viewport change; layouts carry unrecorded width assumptions, and collision gates cannot see text overflowing its own box | 2026-08-19.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/generated-tables-versus-handwritten-prose-drift]] | A CSV-generated table guards its own region only; the authored sentence above it said \"roughly thirteen vendors\" over a list of twelve, caught only by re-reading the rendered output | 2026-08-30.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/arguable-threshold-design]] | Draw the rule on the row and state it in plain English so the domain expert can dispute it; contestability at the point of the flag, not transparency in an appendix | 2026-08-30.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[connections/instrumentation-that-normalizes-the-thing-under-test]] | curl collapsing duplicate Host headers, CRLF normalization, and agent summarization all disqualify the instrument for the property it transforms — a passing result is the dangerous case